VERDICT: SHIP WITH CHANGES (3)

**Q1 — Premise audit**

1. **All 20 refusal-exemption cells are held.**

| Site / destination | CLEAR witness | SET witness |
|---|---|---|
| S1 A | `stip a` | `stip copy`; `latch paint` |
| S1 B | `stip b clr` | `stip b` |
| S1 C | `stip c clr` | `stip c` |
| S1 LIN_A | `stip la clr` | `stip lin a` |
| S1 LIN_B | `stip lb clr` | `stip lin b` |
| S2 A | `src 3`; `latch paint` | `src 4`–`src 7`; `src 3 copy` |
| S2 B | `src b clr` | `src 3 b` |
| S2 C | `src c clr` | `src 3 c` |
| S2 LIN_A | `src la clr` | `src 3 lin` |
| S2 LIN_B | `src lb clr` | `src 3 lin b` |

The original sessions establish A-CLEAR before subsequent SET accesses. Each new paired session starts fresh, invokes S1 once, then S2 once. Those sites have distinct bits; the S1 operation carries source 0 and cannot prime S2. See [regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:255](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:255), [:274](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:274), [:312](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:312), and [src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:182](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:182).

2. **Every new refusal cell would write if exempted.** B/C have their own TLB entries mapped to the painted physical page. Every cell repaints before START and reads afterward. Linear cells select the correct array, target four bytes at `0x30000`, and use depth 8, full BYTEMASK and COPY clear. Escapes therefore reach a tiled BG write or the linear `0x44444444` fill. See [regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:220](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:220), [:283](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:283), [:305](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:305), and [src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1608](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1608), [:1723](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1723).

3. **Crossbit priming is sound for the claimed single-alias mutations.** The accesses set bits 0–5, 6, 7, 8, 10, 9, 11 and 12 before S1 starts. `PRIME_LIT` contains 13 distinct site-specific strings; `xbit primed` checks each string’s presence, rather than accepting any thirteen announcements. The corresponding warning updates use `|=`, so every one of the **65 new-site→old-bit aliases** suppresses a required new-site announcement. Five are packet-reported measurements; the other 60 follow by construction. See [regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:430](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:430) and [:438](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:438).

4. **The strict append-preservation premise is false; the gate premise is true.** New S2 transfers precede the existing scratch store/read at [regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:287](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:287). Thus `src surv` has a changed command prefix, while `src once` counts the expanded session. Existing transfer-paint reads retain their prefixes.

   A read-only, in-memory expansion found **68 unique emitted names**, exactly matching the gate’s 68 unique names; maximum name length is 14. The emitted/green denominators are both 68, and red is pinned to zero at [regress/gate_arm.sh:1499](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_arm.sh:1499).

**Q3 — New-row validity**

**None of the 15 new rows is unable to change under its stated mutant.** The eleven refusal cells observe overwritten paint; the two acceptance cells observe a missing write; `xbit primed` observes a missing priming text; `xbit texts` observes a missing new-site announcement.

Pairing does not confound the named exemption mutations: the first result is read before the second repaint, and each site initially has its own latch clear. However, the paired sessions check only paint, so a *grown S1 guard* can perform the second operation’s refusal without its missing S2 announcement being noticed. That matters to the separate coverage finding below. See [regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:312](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:312).

**Q4 — Records and additional findings**

